# Cursor AI Rules for City Slacker Project

## Project Root Directory
- **IMPORTANT:** The project root is THIS directory (where this .cursorrules file is located)
- **Active Development:** The `web/` subdirectory contains the React web prototype
- **Archived:** The `city-slacker/` subdirectory is an old Unity project (NOT in active development)

## Current Development Phase
- **Phase:** Phase 5 - Content Polish & Enhancement
- **Status:** Ready to Start
- **Entry Point:** Read `CURRENT_PHASE.md` in this directory for complete context
- **Track Details:** `conductor/tracks/phase5_polish_20260123/`

## Directory Structure
```
C:\city-slacker\                    ← YOU ARE HERE (project root)
├── web/                            ← Active React web prototype
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/             ← React components
│   │   │   └── BoardLoop.jsx       ← Main game component
│   │   ├── config/
│   │   │   └── gameBalance.js      ← Game balance config
│   │   └── utils/                  ← Utility functions
│   ├── tests/                      ← Test suites
│   └── package.json
├── conductor/                      ← Project management
│   ├── tracks/                     ← Development tracks
│   │   └── phase5_polish_20260123/ ← Current phase
│   └── workflow.md                 ← Development workflow
├── CURRENT_PHASE.md                ← START HERE for context
├── README.md                       ← Project overview
└── STATUS.md                       ← Current state
```

## Development Workflow
1. **Always start from project root** (where this file is)
2. **Navigate to web/** for all development work
3. **Read CURRENT_PHASE.md** to understand what to work on
4. **Follow TDD workflow** in `conductor/workflow.md`
5. **Update plan.md** as you complete tasks

## Quick Commands
```bash
# From project root:
cd web               # Navigate to active project
npm install          # Install dependencies
npm run dev          # Start dev server
npm test             # Run tests
npm run lint         # Check code quality
```

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend:** React 18, Vite, Tailwind CSS
- **Animation:** Framer Motion
- **Testing:** Vitest (unit), Playwright (E2E)
- **State:** React hooks (no Redux/Context)
- **Storage:** localStorage (no backend yet)

## Development Philosophy
- **TDD:** Write tests first, then implementation
- **Quality:** >80% test coverage required
- **Performance:** 60fps target
- **Accessibility:** WCAG AA compliance

## Current Task
- **Task 5.1:** Enhanced City Transitions (2-3 hours)
- **Details:** See `conductor/tracks/phase5_polish_20260123/plan.md`
- **Specs:** See `conductor/tracks/phase5_polish_20260123/spec.md`

## Important Files
- `web/src/components/BoardLoop.jsx` - Main game component
- `web/src/config/gameBalance.js` - Game balance configuration
- `web/src/utils/saveSystem.js` - Save/load system
- `web/src/utils/sessionAnalytics.js` - Analytics tracking

## Test Status
- **Tests:** 73/73 passing (100%)
- **Coverage:** ~80% on critical paths
- **Target:** >85% coverage for Phase 5

## Code Style
- Use functional components with hooks
- Follow TDD workflow (Red → Green → Refactor)
- Use Tailwind utility classes for styling
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Keep components focused and single-responsibility

## Commit Message Format
```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

Examples:
feat(transitions): Add city transition animations
fix(particles): Resolve memory leak in particle cleanup
test(e2e): Add city progression tests
docs(readme): Update project structure
```

## Quality Gates
Before marking any task complete:
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] Code coverage >80%
- [ ] No linting errors
- [ ] No console errors
- [ ] Performance maintained (60fps)
- [ ] Documentation updated if needed

